to StandardAero, Inc. in September 2024. The company was founded in 1911 and is headquartered in Scottsdale, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul A. McElhinney | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $140,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $758K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["StandardAero, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $9.1B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $234M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.013009525478687906},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $9.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-9514260.22},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing General Dynamics (NYSE:GD) and StandardAero (NYSE:SARO)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/reviewing-general-dynamics-nysegd-and-standardaero-nysesaro.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794574914.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.938,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"StandardAero (SARO) Could Be 16% Undervalued Following Raised 2026 Revenue Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-saro/standardaero/news/standardaero-saro-could-be-16-undervalued-following-raised-2","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794475999.726,"or